Q: Datalist suggestions on input in firefox A: <p>There is <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1882075" rel="nofollow noreferrer">an open request</a> to make datalist show its dropdown in Firefox with only a single click. Until that is implemented, we can use the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLInputElement/showPicker" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>showPicker()</code></a> method to work around this limitation and any similar quirks datalist might have. <code>showPicker()</code> support for datalist <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1767228" rel="nofollow noreferrer">was implemented</a> in Firefox 149, which will be released on 24 March 2026.</p>
<p>Example snippet for Fluxian's HTML, triggering <code>showPicker()</code> for the input element upon focus events:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>let searchList = document.getElementById(&quot;search&quot;);
searchList.addEventListener(&quot;focus&quot;, (e) =&gt; {
  e.currentTarget.showPicker();
});
</code></pre>
